---
import Component from "../../../src/components/BlogPostBody.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for BlogPostBody on an ORDINARY post — the unlocked branch.
//
// BlogPostBody exists to make one decision: ciphertext must never reach the
// markdown renderer. This page is the half of that decision where nothing is
// encrypted, so the component gets out of the way and the article renders. Its
// pair is `BlogPostBody-Locked`, which takes the other branch.
//
// The entry carries no `previewLock`, which is what "ordinary" means here — an
// unlocked PREVIEW takes this same branch, because being unlisted changes where
// a page is linked from, not how it reads once you arrive.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: BlogPostBody</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
    <div id="codeyam-capture" style="padding: var(--space-lg); width: 100%; max-width: var(--content-width);">
      <Component
        post={{
          body: 'Unused on this branch — the markdown arrives as the slot below.',
          data: {
            title: 'Founder Spotlight: Hana Reyes on Building in Climate Hardware',
            date: new Date('2026-07-24'),
          },
        }}
      >
        <p>
          Hana Reyes (Harvard C'14) spent four years inside a utility before deciding the grid's
          storage problem was a hardware problem nobody wanted to own.
        </p>
        <p>
          "Everyone wants to build the software layer," she says. "The software layer is fine. The
          cells are the thing."
        </p>
      </Component>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
